# Named volume for beszel hub persistent data (/beszel_data).
# henrygd/beszel builds FROM scratch with no USER directive, so the image
# runs as root and writes root-owned data here. No User=/Group= — unlike
# letsencrypt.volume (minimus traefik) — because these keys only apply when
# the volume is CREATED: on a host where the volume already exists with
# root-owned content they are silently ignored, and pairing them with
# User=1000 on the container is what broke the hub in #26 (reverted).
[Volume]
